#1113 is fixed and committed as 6dad2f78. yoyo -p --help now sends --help as the prompt instead of printing the help page. -p --version behaves the same way, and bare --help / --version still print and send nothing.

Before the fix: on the built binary, yoyo -p --help printed the help page and exited 0, and -p --version printed the version line.

What changed:
• `cli_config::has_option` now steps over the word after any flag in FLAGS_NEEDING_VALUES, the same way option_split walks argv. So --model --no-color no longer turns colour off.
• The help/version check in `dispatch_sub` used to scan argv itself; it now goes through has_option. That covers all three early checks named in the issue: help/version, main.rs apply_cli_flags and the quiet/print check in parse_args.
• `option_args` is unchanged, because parse_args_with_config needs the flag values it returns.

Tests:
• A table test for has_option:
  • -p --help → false
  • --help → true
  • -p hi --help → true (hi is -p's value and --help is a real flag)
  • -- --help → false
  • --model x --no-color → true
  • --model --no-color → false
  • --system -q → false
• A real-binary test against the stub server: -p --help and -p --version reach it with the word as the prompt.
• Two sabotage checks, run one at a time and both restored: putting back the old has_option body makes the table test fail, and putting back the old dispatch_sub check makes the binary test fail.
• fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test all pass.

What's still broken, now #1114: about 31 other flag checks in cli.rs (parse_args_with_config and the model-config parse) still treat the word after -p as a flag. For example, yoyo -p --print-system-prompt prints the system prompt instead of sending it; I ran that one. The other flags listed in #1114 (--yes, --json and so on) are from a grep and were not each run. That was outside #1113's scope, but this push closes #1113, so I filed #1114 for it first. docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md now describes the fix and points to #1114.

One problem along the way: my first edit_file call pasted a fragment of old text at the end of cli_config.rs. I removed it and re-inserted the test before anything was committed.
